WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:06.480
How do you find the percentage of a given quantity?

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:10.220
I mean something like what is '10% of 30'?

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.040
We go step by step to understand this.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.940
First let's look at '10%'.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.940
We can write '10% as 10 by 100'.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.100
'10 parts out of 100'.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.680
'Of' means 'multiplied by'.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.980
And we write '30' as is.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.380
'10 times 10' is '100'.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.280
And '10 times 3' is '30'.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.700
So this equals '3'.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.040
So '10 percent of 30' is '3'.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.900
But what does this exactly mean?

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.040
Let's understand this with an example.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.760
What it actually means

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:54.740
is '3 out of 30' parts equals '10 percent'.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.760
I have 8 mangoes.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:03.000
'25%' of them have been lying around for too long and are rotten.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.680
So how many mangoes are rotten?

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.640
'25 percent of these 8 mangoes' are no good.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.620
How much is that?

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.880
What do we do in this case?

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.380
Let's see.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.060
The total number of mangoes is '8'.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:22.200
And it says that '25 percent' of the total mangoes are

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.240
unfit for consumption.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:28.180
So '25% of 8 are rotten'.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.480
We use the same technique which we used here.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.140
We write '25 percent' as

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.200
'25 by 100'

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.860
'of' as multiplied by and '8' as is.

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.920
So all we have to do is find '25 by 100'

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.840
multiplied by '8'.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:52.580
'25 times 4 is 100' and '4 times 2 is 8'.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.100
So this 'equals 2'.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:59.780
So we can say that '2 mangoes' out of the '8' are rotten.

